! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 7's COMPARISON test -- the
! REMAINDER of the block programs/ax5b_160105_compare.strap starts.
! PDF pp.72-73, octal 022401.40-022460.40, 92 rows, transcribed
! VERBATIM at the listing's own addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_160_test7_compare_listing.py.  (This deck's listing pages
! carry NO printed page numbers; cite PDF pages only.)
!
! WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AND NOT A SECOND COPY OF p.71.  The task that
! commissioned this transcription named PDF p.71 as the target.  p.71
! is ALREADY in the repo, complete and green: ax5b_160105_compare.strap
! covers 022346.40-022401.00, every row, and
! verify_ax5b_160105_listing.py prints ALL TESTS PASSED for it --
! including the two rows the task quoted as evidence the block was
! untouched, 022371.40 "I6010A BD,$+.32  -ALL INTRPTS EXCEPT AD ENTER
! HERE." and 022372.00 "I60107 BD,$+.32  -AD INTRPTS ENTER HERE."
! Re-transcribing it under a second name would put two files on one
! octal range.  So this file takes the UNCOVERED remainder instead,
! which is also where the interesting part is: p.71 sets the bounds and
! fetches; pp.72-73 are where the COMPARISON's verdict is checked and
! where every error message lives.
!
! WHAT IT PROVES, and it is the deck's own oracle for the half-open
! interval.  The driver on p.71 plants LB = L and UB = L+2 and fetches
! from UB itself with the boundary control bit ONE (signal OUTSIDE),
! expecting a signal.  This file's first half then fetches from UB-1,
! same control bit, and demands NO signal:
!
!     022410.40  BZDFZ,I60111        <- branch on DF OFF is the OK path
!     022411.00  SIC,SEN   -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC 1,
!     022411.40  B,SERS    -CAUSES DF TO BE SET.
!
! UB signals, UB-1 does not, under one and the same control bit.  That
! pair is exactly "up to, but NOT INCLUDING, the address in the upper
! boundary register" (Reference Manual C22-6530-2, printed p.31), and
! it spans this file and the committed one.
!
! THE SECOND HALF IS THE LOWER EDGE, still BC 1: fetch from LB-1 and
! demand a signal.
!
!     022431.00  I60114 BDFZ,I60115  <- branch on DF ON is the OK path
!     022431.40  LX,$X15,3.0  -LB COMP FAILED. FETCH FROM LB-1
!     022432.00  SIC,SEN      -FAILS TO SET DF. IX 15 CONTAINS
!     022432.40  B,SERS       -LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FITCH.
!
! THE p.73 HALF FLIPS THE CONTROL BIT.  Everything on p.72 transmits
! BOUND1 (the word with BIT57 set) into location 3; p.73's
! "TI,1,BOUND0,3.0" at 022442.40 transmits BOUND0 (bit 57 clear) and
! fetches from between the two bounds -- "-FETCH FRM LB+1, UB-1, BC IS
! 0." -- demanding a signal.  So the transcribed range witnesses BOTH
! arms of the control-bit ternary, not one.
!
! BRANCH POLARITY, stated once so it cannot be read backwards: B<IND>
! branches when the indicator is ON, BZ<IND> when it is OFF, a trailing
! Z clears it.  In every check here the BRANCH is the OK path and the
! FALL-THROUGH is the SIC,SEN / B,SERS error pair, and the error text
! names the ANOMALY, not the requirement.  "-CAUSES DF TO BE SET." is
! printed on the path taken when DF WAS set and should not have been.
!
! THE ERROR MESSAGES AND HEADINGS, verbatim with their octal locations
! (read at 600 dpi; see the verify script for the glyph measurements):
!
!   022401.40  -CLR INT 1.
!   022406.00  -RESTORE MY INT.
!   022407.00  -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC IS 1.
!   022410.00  -RESTORE SSIP INT.
!   022411.00  -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC 1,
!   022411.40  -CAUSES DF TO BE SET.
!   022412.40  -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC 1,
!   022413.00  -CAUSES AD INTERRUPT.
!   022413.40  -RESTORE SSIP INT.
!   022422.00  -FETCH FROM LB-1, BC IS 1.
!   022424.40  -DID WE INTRPT LAST TIME THRU.
!   022426.00  -INTERRUPTED TWICE ON A FETCH BELOW
!   022426.40  -LB,IX 15 CONTAINS CONTENTS OF
!   022427.00  -LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FETCH.
!   022430.00  -AD INTERRUPT ONCE ON FETCH
!   022430.40  -BELOW LB.
!   022431.40  -LB COMP FAILED. FETCH FROM LB-1
!   022432.00  -FAILS TO SET DF. IX 15 CONTAINS
!   022432.40  -LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FITCH.
!   022434.40  -TO SSIP
!   022435.40  -CLR INT 2.
!   022444.40  -FETCH FRM LB+1, UB-1, BC IS 0.
!   022447.00  -DID WE INTRPT LAST TIME THRU.
!   022450.40  -INTERRUPTED TWICE ON A FETCH BETWEEN
!   022451.00  -UB AND LB, IX 15 CONTAINS CONTENTS OF
!   022451.40  -LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FETCH.
!   022452.40  -AD INTERRUPT ONCE ON FETCH
!   022453.00  -BETWEEN UB AND LB.
!   022454.00  -BETWEEN UB AND LB COMP FAILED. FETCH
!   022454.40  -BETWEEN THE TWO FAILS TO SET DF. IX 15
!   022455.00  -CONTAINS LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FETCH.
!   022457.00  -TO SSIP.
!   022457.40  -TERMINATE.
!   022460.00  -CLR INT 3.
!
! "FITCH" at 022432.40 is the deck's, not the scan's -- the glyph is a
! clean bare stroke, identical to the I in "TIME" three words earlier,
! and the SAME message spells "FETCH FROM LB-1" correctly one line
! above.  "FRM" at 022444.40 is likewise the deck's.  Note also
! "-TO SSIP" at 022434.40 with NO period where 022457.00 has one.
!
! ONE ROW LOOKS LIKE A BUG IN IBM'S OWN DIAGNOSTIC.  At 022452.40 the
! deck writes "SV,$X14,I60AD3" where its two parallel blocks write
! $X13 (022430.00 "SV,$X13,I60AD2", 022460.40 "SV,$X13,I60AD3"), and
! the printed machine code agrees with the source: 23064.35 30 against
! 23063.73 30 / 23064.33 30, an index field of 14 against 13.  The row
! is transcribed AS PRINTED.  Whether it is a typo that survived into
! the shipped deck is not decidable from this page; the observation is
! that the bits and the letters agree.
!
! ENCODING ONLY, same reason as the p.71 half: the block cannot run
! without SSIP's save/restore at 001301/001304/001310/001311, the
! interruption table I60IT at 023201.00, and BOUND0/BOUND1 at
! 023302/023303.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: one, the same as the p.71 file's.  Numeric labels are
! prefixed "L" (160110, 16011A, 160210, 160111 ... 160120, plus the
! externals 160107, 16010A, 160121, 160122, 160AD1, 160AD2, 160AD3).
! "%8(0)777777.40" is written "(8)777777.40" and "0%$X2(0)" is written
! "0($X2)", exactly as ax5b_160105_compare.strap writes them.  Nothing
! else is changed; every external is given by SYN at the address this
! block's own rows print for it.

I60107 SYN, (8)22372.0
I6010A SYN, (8)22371.40
I60121 SYN, (8)22461.0
I60122 SYN, (8)22506.40
I60AD1 SYN, (8)23063.0
I60AD2 SYN, (8)23063.40
I60AD3 SYN, (8)23064.0
BOUND0  SYN, (8)23302.0
BOUND1  SYN, (8)23303.0
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0
        SLC, (8)22401.40
I60110 Z,   $X13                ! -CLR INT 1.
        SV,  $X13, I60AD1
        TI,  1, BOUND1, 3.0
        LVI, $X13, I60210
        SVA, $X13, I60107
        LVI, $X3, I6011A
        SVA, $X3, I6010A
        V-I, $X2, 1.0
        SR,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE MY INT.
        BE,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, 0($X2)        ! -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC IS 1.
I6011A BD,  $+.32
        SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE SSIP INT.
        BZDFZ, I60111
        SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC 1,
        B,   SERS                ! -CAUSES DF TO BE SET.
        B,   I60111
I60210 SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH FROM UB-1, BC 1,
        B,   SERS                ! -CAUSES AD INTERRUPT.
        SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE SSIP INT.
I60111 LVI, $X13, I60112
        SVA, $X13, I60107
        LVI, $X3, I60114
        SVA, $X3, I6010A
        BDFZ, $+.32
        Z,   $MASK
        Z,   $IND
        TI,  1, BOUND1, 3.0
        V-I, $X2, 2.0
        SR,  $X1, $IA
        BE,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, 0($X2)        ! -FETCH FROM LB-1, BC IS 1.
        BD,  $+.32
        SV,  $X1, $IA
        BD,  I60114
I60112 SV,  $X1, $IA
        LV,  $X13, I60AD2       ! -DID WE INTRPT LAST TIME THRU.
        BXVZ, I60113
        LX,  $X15, 3.0
        SIC, SEN                 ! -INTERRUPTED TWICE ON A FETCH BELOW
        B,   SERS                ! -LB,IX 15 CONTAINS CONTENTS OF
        B,   I60122             ! -LOCN 3.0 AT TIME OF FETCH.
I60113 V+I, $X13, (8)777777.40
